    "raw_content": "The bug is in `worker/outbox_worker.py`. The `outbox.ack(row[\"id\"])` call is outside the `try/except` block, meaning it executes even when `publish` raises an exception. This causes poison events (and any other failed publishes) to be acknowledged and thus lost, preventing retries.\n\nThe fix is to move `outbox.ack(row[\"id\"])` inside the `try` block, so it only runs after a successful publish. This ensures that failed publishes leave the row unacked (since `ack` is not called), allowing it to be retried in a later batch claim (since `claim_batch` filters on `not r.get(\"acked\")`).\n\n<arch_final>\n{\"patch\": \"--- a/worker/outbox_worker.py\\n+++ b/worker/outbox_worker.py\\n@@ -25,9 +25,9 @@ def process_once(publish: Callable[[dict], None] | None = None) -> dict[str, Any\\n     for row in batch:\\n         try:\\n             publish(row)\\n-            outbox.mark_published(row[\\\"id\\\"])\\n-            ok += 1\\n-        except Exception:\\n-            failed += 1\\n-        outbox.ack(row[\\\"id\\\"])\\n+            outbox.mark_published(row[\\\"id\\\"])\\n+            outbox.ack(row[\\\"id\\\"])\\n+            ok += 1\\n+        except Exception:\\n+            failed += 1\\n     return {\\\"ok\\\": ok, \\\"failed\\\": failed, \\\"batch\\\": len(batch)}\\n\\\\ No newline at end of file\"}\n</arch_final>"
